*The following is OfficeFloor's own agent guidance for this stack, included verbatim
from <https://officefloor.net/AGENTS.md>. It is part of the OfficeFloor architecture.*

## OfficeFloor REST endpoints

Applies when adding or changing REST endpoints. This project serves REST through
OfficeFloor Function Injection, **not** Spring MVC controllers: each endpoint is a
pipeline of small function classes wired together in YAML.

- Requires the OfficeFloor Spring Boot starter in the build:
  `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` (Spring Boot 4.x) or
  `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-3-starter` (Spring Boot 3.x). Without it these YAML
  files are inert. (Rules below track these starter versions.)
- Define each endpoint as a YAML file under `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/`,
  named `<path>.<METHOD>.yml` (e.g. `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` → `PUT /owners/{ownerId}`).
- One small function class per step; compose steps with `next:` and `outputs:`.
- Do NOT generate `@RestController`, `@GetMapping` or `@PostMapping`.
- Transactions: `govern: [ transaction ]` on steps, not `@Transactional`.
- Errors: a handler YAML in `officefloor/escalation/`, not `@ControllerAdvice`.

### Worked example — `PUT /owners/{ownerId}`

The whole shape of an endpoint. The sections after this one are the reference.

`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`

```yaml
# First step runs first. Validate before Load so an invalid body is a 400,
# not masked by a 404 for a missing owner.
validate:
  class: com.example.owner.ValidateOwner
  next: load
load:
  class: com.example.owner.LoadOwner
  next: apply
apply:
  class: com.example.owner.ApplyOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save
save:
  class: com.example.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond
respond:
  class: com.example.owner.RespondWithOwner
```

```java
// One public method each. State moves by Out<T> (set) → @Val (read), matched by type.
public class ValidateOwner {
  public void validate(@RequestBody @Valid OwnerRequest request, Out<OwnerRequest> body) {
    body.set(request); // body read once here; republished for later steps
  }
}
public class LoadOwner {
  public void load(@PathVariable("ownerId") int ownerId, OwnerRepository repository,
      Out<Owner> ownerOut) throws OwnerNotFoundException {
    Owner owner = repository.findById(ownerId);
    if (owner == null) throw new OwnerNotFoundException(ownerId); // handled below
    expect(await ui.exportCsv(pg_uma)).toBe("name,grade,retired-from,due-total\nAda,A,,2.00\nBen,B,2026-03-05,0.00\n");
    expect(await ui.exportClaims(pg_uma)).toBe("person,number,date,amount,due,status,period\nAda,FY2026-1,2026-03-01,10.00,2.00,OPEN,\nBen,FY2026-2,2026-03-05,5.00,1.00,OPEN,\n");
    expect(await ui.exportPools(pg_uma)).toBe("pool,member,share,cut\nP1,Ada,100.00,20.00\n");
    await ui.setAsOf(pg_uma, "2026-03-01");
    expect(await ui.exportCsv(pg_uma)).toBe("name,grade,retired-from,due-total\nAda,A,,1.00\nBen,B,,0.00\n");
    expect(await ui.exportClaims(pg_uma)).toBe("person,number,date,amount,due,status,period\nAda,FY2026-1,2026-03-01,10.00,1.00,OPEN,\n");
    expect(await ui.exportPools(pg_uma)).toBe("pool,member,share,cut\nP1,Ada,100.00,10.00\n");
    await ui.clearAsOf(pg_uma);
    expect(await ui.exportCsv(pg_uma)).toBe("name,grade,retired-from,due-total\nAda,A,,2.00\nBen,B,2026-03-05,0.00\n");
  });
  test("as of exports scenario 1", { tag: '@functionality' }, async ({ browser }) => {
    const sheet = ui.sheetId();
    const pg_uma = await ui.userPage(browser, "uma", sheet);
    await ui.setToday(pg_uma, "2026-03-20");
    expect(await ui.setRole(pg_uma, "vic", "steward")).toBe(true);
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "clerk-limit", "3.00");
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "terms", "30");
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "late-pct", "5.00");
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "cap", "5.00");
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "note-threshold", "1.00");
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "grace-A", "2");
    await ui.loadSheet(pg_uma, `${sheet}-p`);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "A", "pct": "5.00"})).toBe(true);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "B", "pct": "7.50"})).toBe(true);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "C", "pct": "7.50"})).toBe(true);
    const p_cam = ui.must(await ui.addPerson(pg_uma, {"name": "Cam", "grade": "C"}));
    await ui.loadSheet(pg_uma, sheet);
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "parent", `${sheet}-p`);
    await ui.setSetting(pg_uma, "review-threshold", "1.50");
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "A", "pct": "33.33"})).toBe(true);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "B", "pct": "20.00"})).toBe(true);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "C", "pct": "12.50"})).toBe(true);
    expect(await ui.setRate(pg_uma, {"grade": "C", "pct": "7.50", "from": "2026-03-16", "to": "2026-03-12"})).toBe(false);
    expect(await ui.addPeriod(pg_uma, {"name": "P1", "from": "2026-03-01", "to": "2026-03-15"})).toBe(true);
    const p_ada = ui.must(await ui.addPerson(pg_uma, {"name": "Ada", "grade": "C"}));
    expect(await ui.addPerson(pg_uma, {"name": "Cam", "grade": "A", "terms": "3", "contact": "ADA@X"})).toBeNull();
